.TH RAINDROPS 1
.SH NAME
raindrops \- falling-water simulation demo
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/raindrops
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Raindrops
is a port of the TempleOS falling-water demo
.BR RainDrops .
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Drops of water rain from the top of the window and flow: a drop falls
while the pixel below it is empty, otherwise it slides sideways and
down when it can, so water pools in the two red funnels, piles up on
the red block and the long ledge, and runs off the bottom of the
window.
.PP
Each funnel has a small hole at its vertex.
Holding
.B 1
or
.B 2
opens the corresponding hole, draining the pool above it; releasing
the key closes it again.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF space
.TP
.B 1 (hold)
Open the upper funnel's hole
.TP
.B 2 (hold)
Open the lower funnel's hole
.TP
.B Enter
Restart: clear all water
.TP
.B Esc / q
Quit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/raindrops.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
